# Required for Module 1
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Required for Module 4 (inquiry form spam protection)
# For local development, use Cloudflare's published always-pass test
# keys rather than a real site: sitekey 1x00000000000000000000AA,
# secret 1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA. Replace both with your
# real Turnstile site's keys before deploying anywhere public.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA

# The action value both the widget and the server's verification check
# against. Cloudflare's dummy siteverify backend (used with the test
# keys above) echoes back a fixed "test" action regardless of what the
# widget actually requested — so local dev must set this to "test" to
# match, or every Turnstile verification will fail on an action mismatch.
# PRODUCTION MUST set this to submit_inquiry once real Turnstile keys are
# configured — leaving it as "test" against a real site provides no
# actual action-binding protection.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_ACTION=test

# Required for Module 4 (privileged server-only client — see
# src/lib/supabase/admin.ts). This is the Supabase project's SECRET key
# (Settings → API Keys → Secret key, sb_secret_...) — NEVER the
# publishable key, NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, and NEVER used anywhere
# except server-only code (Server Actions, Route Handlers). It bypasses
# Row Level Security entirely. Left blank here intentionally — fill in
# your own project's value locally, never commit a real value to source
# control.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional, deployment-specific (Module 4). Leave blank/unset unless you
# have specifically verified, against your own infrastructure's
# documentation, that the header you name here is guaranteed to be set
# or overwritten by trusted edge/proxy infrastructure and cannot simply
# be supplied by the client itself. The configured header MUST contain
# exactly one edge-verified client IP — never an X-Forwarded-For-style
# comma-separated chain; a value containing a comma is rejected outright
# rather than guessing which position in the chain to trust. Do NOT set
# this to x-forwarded-for on the assumption that it's automatically
# trustworthy or that taking one entry from it is safe — per the
# X-Forwarded-For convention, each hop appends its own observed address
# rather than replacing the header outright, so a client can prepend a
# fabricated entry before any real proxy ever sees the request, and
# without an explicitly configured trusted-proxy-hop count there is no
# generically safe way to know which entry to trust. When this is left
# unset (the default), IP-based rate limiting on the inquiry form is
# simply skipped — visitor-ID and normalized-email based rate limiting
# remain fully active regardless, so leaving this blank is a safe
# default, not a coverage gap. See the extended comment above
# getClientIp() in src/lib/inquiries/actions.ts for the full reasoning.
TRUSTED_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=

# Documented for future modules — leave blank, no value needed yet
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=    # added in Module 7
# META_CONVERSIONS_API_TOKEN=   # added in Module 7
